// 31 bits fill a 4-byte unit; the next 33 would need an 8-byte unit beginning at
// byte 3, inside the bytes the first unit already owns. Two emitted members that
// overlap cannot be expressed, so the layout is refused rather than emitted in a
// form that disagrees with it.
struct D { a: u31, b: u33 }
fn main() i32 { return 0; }
